"Create a Kids Profile (https://help.audible.com/s/article/create-a-kids-profile?language=en_US)\nciteturn997view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.audible.com/s/article/create-a-kids-profile?language=en_US\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 130\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Ask A Question Kids Profile Profiles\nL13: ## Create a Kids Profile\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 9, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Create a Kids Profile\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: create-a-kids-profile\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: There’s no minimum age requirement for a Kids Profile and anyone with an Audible account with an Amazon login can create a single Kids Profile to share titles for kids and featured editorial lists with children right from their Library—regardless of membership and as long as you, as the account holder, have access to the titles.\nL29: This will allow kids to listen to only the titles you choose. You can share titles you’ve purchased with cash or credit as well as any titles for kids included in your membership, and there’s no limit to how many titles you can share.\nL30: \nL31: \nL32: \nL33: Kids Profile is only available in the Audible app for iOS and Android and on the Audible website. If you are using Audible on Fire Tablet, Kindle or Echo device, please create a Child account within 【1†Amazon Family Library】.\nL34: \nL35: Notes:\nL36:   * Your child only has access to titles you directly share with them.\nL37:   * Some titles are restricted from sharing, such as audiobooks with erotica content, podcasts with ads and titles with Virtual Voice narration.\nL38:   * Kids Profiles don’t get access to credits or selections. You’ll need to purchase titles with your credits first, then share it to your Kids Profile.\nL39: \nL40: In this article:\nL41:   * 【2†What is a Kids Profile?】\nL42:   * 【3†How do I create a Kids Profile?】\nL43:   * 【4†Can I create more than one Kids Profile?】\nL44:   * 【5†Can multiple kids listen to my Kids Profile?】\nL45:   * 【6†Why was a Kids Profile automatically created on my account?】\nL46: ## What is a Kids Profile?\nL47: \nL48: Kids Profile is a new feature for Audible customers that helps parents share their love of stories with their children right from the Audible app and the Audible website. With access to only those titles and lists that you choose to share, your child can easily listen from the Audible app whenever and wherever they choose.\nL49: ## How do I create a Kids Profile?\nL50: \nL51: You can create a Kids Profile from the Profile tab in the Audible app or on the Audible site from your Membership details.\nL52: \nL53: ### In the app\nL54: \nL55:   * Go to your Profile.\nL56:   * Select Create a Kids Profile.\nL57: ### On desktop\nL58: \nL59:   * Go to the Audible site and sign in.\nL60:   * Select your name on the top navigation.\nL61:   * Select Membership details.\nL62:   * Select 【7†Profiles†www.audible.com】.\nL63:   * Select Create a Kids Profile.\nL64: \nL65: If you want to learn more about who to log into your Kid Profile after it was created please visit 【8†Listen with a Kids Profile】.\nL66: ## Can I create more than one Kids profile?\nL67: \nL68: No. You can only create 1 Kids Profile per 【9†Amazon Family†www.amazon.com】 or Audible account. If you're part of an Amazon Family and a Kids Profile has already been created for a member of your Amazon Family, you won't be able to create a new one until the existing profile is deleted.\nL69: ## Can multiple kids listen to my Kids Profile?\nL70: \nL71: Yes. You can create 1 Kids Profile per account that can be accessed on multiple devices. Multiple children can use this same Kids Profile simultaneously without interrupting each other's listening progress.\nL72: ## Why was a Kids Profile automatically created on my account?\nL73: Audible may have received notice that you are, or the user of your device is, under the age of 18. New legislation requires online services to provide enhanced protection for users under 18. If the app store account accessing the Audible app is registered to a child under 18, the Audible app experience may now default to the Kids Profile in certain US states. The Kids Profile is a kid-friendly space where you can share only the titles you choose from your Library.\nL74: You can continue to access your Audible account and manage any titles you'd like to 【10†share with your Kids Profile】 from the Audible app on your personal device or the Audible site.\nL75: For questions on how the app store for your device applies age signals, please contact your app store customer service.\nL76: Did this answer your question?\nL77: \nL78: 【11†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL79: \nL80: \nL81: \nL82: 【12†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL83: \nL84:  Back to top\nL85: \nL86: 【13†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL87: \nL88: 【14†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL89: ## Need more assistance?\nL90: \nL91: 【15†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL92: \nL93: \nL94: \nL95: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL96: \nL97: \nL98: \nL99: Worst\nL100: \nL101: 1\nL102: \nL103: 2\nL104: \nL105: 3\nL106: \nL107: 4\nL108: \nL109: 5\nL110: \nL111: 6\nL112: \nL113: 7\nL114: \nL115: Best\nL116: \nL117: \nL118: \nL119: Region\nL120: \nL121: United States\nL122: \nL123: Language\nL124: \nL125: English\nL126: \nL127: Loading\nL128: \nL129: Create a Kids Profile 【16†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nListen with a Kids Profile (https://help.audible.com/s/article/listen-with-a-kids-profile?language=en_US)\nciteturn997view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.audible.com/s/article/listen-with-a-kids-profile?language=en_US\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 115\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Ask A Question Kids Profile Profiles\nL13: ## Listen with a Kids Profile\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 9, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Listen with a Kids Profile\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: listen-with-a-kids-profile\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: A Kids Profile is a listening space for kids in the Audible app that allows kids to listen to only the titles you choose. You can share titles you’ve purchased with cash or credit as well as any titles for kids included in your membership, and there’s no limit to how many titles you can share.\nL28: Once set up, your child can play any title that you have shared with them. They’ll also be able to organize these titles in lists, and play through lists.\nL29: Kids Profile is only available in the Audible app for iOS and Android and on the Audible website. If you are using Audible on Fire Tablet, Kindle or Echo device, please create a Child account within 【1†Amazon Family Library】.\nL30: \nL31: Notes:\nL32: \nL33:   * Your child will need to reset their listening position each time they switch listening between devices.\nL34:   * Each Audible account can 【2†create 1 Kids Profile.】\nL35:   * Your child only has access to titles you directly share with them.\nL36: \nL37: In this article:\nL38:   * 【3†Can multiple kids listen to on my Kids Profile?】\nL39:   * 【4†Can I change the narration speed on my Kids Profile?】\nL40:   * 【5†How do I switch to my Kids Profile?】\nL41:   * 【6†Why am I unable to switch out of my Kids Profile?】\nL42: ## Can multiple kids listen to my Kids Profile?\nL43: \nL44: Yes. You can sign in to your Kids Profile on multiple devices, and more than 1 child can be using the Kids Profile at the same time without interrupting each other’s listening progress.\nL45: Note: Anyone can listen on a Kids Profile, but only titles for kids can be shared to it.\nL46: ## Can I change the narration speed for my Kids Profile?\nL47: \nL48: Narration speed can be changed in the Kids Profile. Note that the Kids Profile shares 【7†narration speed settings】 with your primary Audible account for that specific device.\nL49: ## How do I switch to my Kids Profile?\nL50: \nL51: You can switch to your Kids Profile anytime from the Audible app.\nL52: Note: You’ll have to sign in with your Amazon email and password to access your adult profile again. To keep your adult profile inaccessible to your child, make sure you do not have any cached login credentials on the device that your child uses to access the Kids Profile.\nL53: In the app\nL54: \nL55:   1. Go to your Profile in the app.\nL56:   2. Select your name in the drop-down.\nL57:   3. Select Kids.\nL58: ## Why am I unable to switch out of my Kids Profile?\nL59: If you are not able to switch out of the Kids Profile, it may mean Audible received a notice that you are, or the user of your device is, under the age of 18. New legislation requires online services to provide enhanced protection for users under 18. If the app store account accessing the Audible app is registered to a child under 18, the Audible app experience may now default to the Kids Profile in certain US states.\nL60: Parents/account holders can continue to access the Audible account and manage titles they’d like 【8†share with the Kids Profile】 from the Audible app on their personal device or the Audible site. For questions on how the app store for your device applies age signals, please contact your app store customer service.\nL61: Did this answer your question?\nL62: \nL63: 【9†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL64: \nL65: \nL66: \nL67: 【10†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL68: \nL69:  Back to top\nL70: \nL71: 【11†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL72: \nL73: 【12†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL74: ## Need more assistance?\nL75: \nL76: 【13†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL77: \nL78: \nL79: \nL80: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL81: \nL82: \nL83: \nL84: Worst\nL85: \nL86: 1\nL87: \nL88: 2\nL89: \nL90: 3\nL91: \nL92: 4\nL93: \nL94: 5\nL95: \nL96: 6\nL97: \nL98: 7\nL99: \nL100: Best\nL101: \nL102: \nL103: \nL104: Region\nL105: \nL106: United States\nL107: \nL108: Language\nL109: \nL110: English\nL111: \nL112: Loading\nL113: \nL114: Listen with a Kids Profile 【14†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nShare with a Kids Profile (https://help.audible.com/s/article/share-with-a-kids-profile?language=en_US)\nciteturn997view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.audible.com/s/article/share-with-a-kids-profile?language=en_US\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 143\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Ask A Question Kids Profile Profiles\nL13: ## Share with a Kids Profile\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 9, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Share with a Kids Profile\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: share-with-a-kids-profile\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: \nL29: \nL30: Kids Profile is only available in the Audible app for iOS and Android and on the Audible website. If you are using Audible on a Fire Tablet, a Kindle, or an Echo device, please create a Child account within 【1†Amazon Family Library】.\nL31: You can share audiobooks, podcast episodes, and featured editorial lists for kids included in your membership, as well as any titles you have purchased for kids with credits or debit or credit card, right from your Library. There's no limit to how many titles you can share.\nL32: \nL33: Notes:\nL34:   * Some titles are restricted from sharing, such as erotica audiobooks, content with ads, and titles narrated with Virtual Voice narration.\nL35:   * Kids Profiles don't get access to credits. You'll need to purchase titles with your credit first, then share it to your Kids Profile.\nL36:   * Content cannot be shared from a device locked to a Kids Profile. The adult account holder must share content from their own device or from 【2†Audible.com†www.audible.com】. To learn more, please visit 【3†Create a Kids Profile】.\nL37: In this article:\nL38: \nL39:   * 【4†How do I share an audiobook with my Kids Profile?】\nL40:   * 【5†Can I share a podcast episode with my Kids Profile?】\nL41:   * 【6†How do I share a list to my Kids Profile?】\nL42:   * 【7†What happens to titles I shared if I cancel or pause my membership?】\nL43:   * 【8†Why is sharing not available for some titles and lists?】\nL44: ## How do I share an audiobook with my Kids Profile?\nL45: \nL46: You can share audiobooks with your Kids Profile from your Library.\nL47: \nL48: In the app\nL49: \nL50:   1. If you haven't already, add the audiobook to your Library.\nL51:   2. Go to the audiobook in your Library.\nL52:   3. Select the 3-dot More menu.\nL53:   4. Select Share with Kids Profile.\nL54: \nL55: On desktop\nL56:   1. Go to the 【2†Audible site†www.audible.com】 and sign in.\nL57:   2. If you haven't already, add the audiobook to your Library.\nL58:   3. Go to the audiobook in your Library.\nL59:   4. Select Share with Kids Profile.\nL60: ## Can I share a podcast episode with my Kids Profile?\nL61: \nL62: Yes. You can share Audible Original podcast episodes with your Kids Profile from your Library anytime.\nL63: \nL64: In the app\nL65: \nL66:   1. If you haven't already, add the podcast episode to your Library.\nL67:   2. Go to the podcast episode in the Podcasts section of your Library.\nL68:   3. Select the 3-dot More menu.\nL69:   4. Select Share with Kids Profile.\nL70: ## How do I share a list to my Kids Profile?\nL71: \nL72: To share a list with your Kids Profile, all podcast episodes and audiobooks within it must be owned or included in your membership and for kids. If you don't own or have access to all titles in the list, it will show as \"Partially shared\" in your Library.\nL73: \nL74: In the app\nL75:   1. If you haven't already, save the kids list to your Lists.\nL76:   2. Go to Lists in your Library.\nL77:   3. Select the 3-dot More menu for the list you want to share.\nL78:   4. Select Share with Kids Profile.\nL79: ## What happens to titles I shared if I cancel or pause my membership?\nL80: \nL81: When you cancel your membership, any audiobooks or podcast episodes you had access to as part of your Audible membership will be locked in your Library as well as your Kids Profile. Any titles you purchased with cash or credit will still be available.\nL82: When you pause your membership, any shared audiobooks or podcasts that are included with your membership will also be locked until your membership resumes. Any titles you purchased with cash or credit will still be available.\nL83: ## Why is sharing not available for some titles and lists?\nL84: \nL85: There are a few reasons that sharing a title or list to your Kids Profile isn't available:\nL86: \nL87:   * You don't own or have access to the audiobook or podcast episode.\nL88:   * The audiobook or podcast episode can't be shared with a Kids Profile.\nL89:   * The list includes titles that can't be shared with a Kids Profile.\nL90:   * The title is recorded with Virtual Voice narration.\nL91: \nL92: Did this answer your question?\nL93: \nL94: 【9†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL95: 【10†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL96: \nL97:  Back to top\nL98: \nL99: 【11†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL100: \nL101: 【12†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL102: ## Need more assistance?\nL103: \nL104: 【13†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL105: \nL106: \nL107: \nL108: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL109: \nL110: \nL111: \nL112: Worst\nL113: \nL114: 1\nL115: \nL116: 2\nL117: \nL118: 3\nL119: \nL120: 4\nL121: \nL122: 5\nL123: \nL124: 6\nL125: \nL126: 7\nL127: \nL128: Best\nL129: \nL130: \nL131: \nL132: Region\nL133: \nL134: United States\nL135: \nL136: Language\nL137: \nL138: English\nL139: \nL140: Loading\nL141: \nL142: Share with a Kids Profile 【14†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDelete a Kids Profile (https://help.audible.com/s/article/delete-a-kids-profile?language=en_US)\nciteturn997view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.audible.com/s/article/delete-a-kids-profile?language=en_US\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 118\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Ask A Question Kids Profile Profiles\nL13: ## Delete a Kids Profile\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 9, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Delete a Kids Profile\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: delete-a-kids-profile\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: You can delete your Kids Profile from your account anytime in the app or on the Audible site.\nL29: Note:\nL30:   * Deleting your Kids Profile will delete all data associated with the Kids Profile.\nL31:   * Deleting your Kids Profile on Audible has no impact on any child accounts in your Amazon Family. For more information on Amazon Family Library sharing, please see our article 【1†Manage Amazon Family Library Sharing†help.audible.co.uk】.\nL32: \nL33: In this article:\nL34:   * 【2†How do I delete my Kids Profile?】\nL35:   * 【3†Can I restore a deleted Kids Profile?】\nL36:   * 【4†What happens to titles I’ve shared to my Kids Profile when I delete it?】\nL37: ## How do I delete my Kids Profile?\nL38: \nL39: You can delete your Kids Profile from the Profile tab in the Audible app or on the Audible site from your Account details anytime.\nL40: Note: This action is permanent and there’s no way to restore shared titles or listen history after you’ve deleted your Kids Profile. Deleting your Kids Profile will delete all personal data within the Kids Profile.\nL41: ### In the app\nL42: \nL43:   * Go to your Profile.\nL44:   * Select Manage Kids Profile.\nL45:   * Select Delete profile.\nL46:   * Confirm that you’d like to delete your Kids Profile.\nL47: \nL48: ### On desktop\nL49: \nL50:   * Go to the Audible site and sign in.\nL51:   * Select your name on the top navigation\nL52:   * Select Membership details.\nL53:   * Select 【5†Profiles†www.audible.com】.\nL54:   * Select Delete profile to the right of the Kids Profile.\nL55:   * Confirm that you’d like to delete your Kids Profile.\nL56: ## Can I restore a deleted Kids Profile?\nL57: \nL58: No, once a Kids Profile is deleted, all personal data within that profile will be deleted permanently. If you create a new Kids Profile, you’ll have to re-share any previously shared titles or lists again.\nL59: ## What happens to titles I’ve shared to my Kids Profile when I delete it?\nL60: \nL61: Your Kids Profile and all personal data will be permanently deleted, but any titles or lists you shared with the Kids Profile will remain in your Library.\nL62: \nL63: \nL64: Did this answer your question?\nL65: \nL66: 【6†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL67: \nL68: \nL69: \nL70: 【7†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL71: \nL72:  Back to top\nL73: \nL74: 【8†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL75: \nL76: 【9†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL77: ## Need more assistance?\nL78: \nL79: 【10†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL80: \nL81: \nL82: \nL83: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL84: \nL85: \nL86: \nL87: Worst\nL88: \nL89: 1\nL90: \nL91: 2\nL92: \nL93: 3\nL94: \nL95: 4\nL96: \nL97: 5\nL98: \nL99: 6\nL100: \nL101: 7\nL102: \nL103: Best\nL104: \nL105: \nL106: \nL107: Region\nL108: \nL109: United States\nL110: \nL111: Language\nL112: \nL113: English\nL114: \nL115: Loading\nL116: \nL117: Delete a Kids Profile 【11†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n"
